        "length": 123.0,
        "width": 74.0,
        "height": 29.0
      },
      "corner_radius_mm": 13.0,
      "display": {
        "face": "front",
        "x_pct": 50.0,
        "y_pct": 32.0
      },
      "display_window_mm": {
        "width": 46.0,
        "height": 22.0
      },
      "intake": {
        "face": "front",
        "x_pct": 50.0,
        "y_pct": 76.0
      },
      "usb": {
        "face": "bottom",
        "x_pct": 50.0,
        "y_pct": 50.0
      },
      "cmf": {
        "material": "PC-ABS",
        "finish": "textured_heavy",
        "color": "high-visibility safety orange (RAL 2003-ish), UV-stabilised masterbatch, matte non-glare",
        "secondary_ops": [
          "tpe_overmold",
          "pad_print",
          "laser_etch"
        ]
      },
      "intent_anchors": [
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA1",
          "statement": "Keep the soft-pebble convex form with no flat side walls; the rounded body is the primary drop-energy distributor and must not be flattened for assembly convenience.",
          "category": "form",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA2",
          "statement": "Preserve the perimeter armour bead at mid-height as a continuous rub rail; it is the first contact point in a 1.5 m drop and protects the front display window and rear sensor pod.",
          "category": "durability",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA3",
          "statement": "Preserve the two flank TPE overmould grip pads at their stated height and extent; they are the glove-friendly, wet-hand grip interface and must not be reduced to decorative inserts.",
          "category": "usability",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA4",
          "statement": "Preserve the front intake as a recessed grille backed by an ePTFE membrane vent plus perimeter gasket; open area must stay >=15% of the grille aperture while retaining IP65.",
          "category": "durability",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA5",
          "statement": "Preserve the single downward-facing USB-C port with a captive silicone flap; do not relocate to a side face, where it would break the pebble section and the gasket line.",
          "category": "usability",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA6",
          "statement": "Hold the UV-stabilised high-visibility orange PC-ABS in textured_heavy; colour and texture are the visibility and grip system together, not a cosmetic choice.",
          "category": "cmf",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA7",
          "statement": "Keep the display window recessed 0.8 mm below the surrounding bead with a 12 mm minimum bezel-to-edge distance so the window glass is never a drop contact point.",
          "category": "durability",
          "must_preserve": true
        }
      ],
      "rationale": "The pebble silhouette is chosen because a continuously curved body has no stress-raising corners and spreads 1.5 m drop loads over a large radius, which is the cheapest way to buy durability inside an CNY 18 BOM. PC-ABS with a textured_heavy finish gives the best impact/UV-stiffness balance among the allowed materials while staying mouldable in a two-plate tool with no side actions; the TPE overmould is the one cost concession that directly satisfies the grippy, glove-friendly requirement and also acts as a secondary drop bumper. The mid-height armour bead is deliberately the widest section (74 mm) so impact energy is absorbed by the rail before it reaches the display or the rear sensor boss. The front face is organised display-up / intake-down so the user's thumb never covers the intake when holding the unit in the field, and the intake recess keeps the ePTFE membrane out of direct rain and dust impingement. USB is on the bottom face behind a captive flap because a bottom port can be sealed with a simple planar gasket, whereas a side port would cut through the pebble's curved wall and require a more expensive seal. High-visibility orange is taken as the default from open question Q1; if yellow is later preferred, only the masterbatch changes and no tooling or anchor is affected. Cost sits above the CNY 12.55 floor mainly through the TPE overmould and ePTFE vent, which are the two features that make the durability and IP65 promises real rather than nominal."
    },
